WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:07.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello everyone my name is nari and as a  continuation of my series where i write  these pocket pieces i wrote something  influenced by the funk genre this week  thank you to paul for suggesting this  idea as a classical musician i wasn't  exposed to funk music until very  recently so first i had to spend some  time deliberately listening to some  recordings  here are a few things i took a mental  note of  [Music]  there is a very strong emphasis on the  downbeat  the overall subdivision of the pulse is  made up of even sets of notes instead of  odd  often times a short pattern made up of  an odd number of notes is repeated and  scattered over this pulse  and lastly the harmonic direction  generally seems to want to sit  comfortably in its place without moving  in too many directions  i tried to keep all of these things in  mind for my piece but i wasn't so strict  about keeping a steady pulse a form and  was only able to try to imitate the sort  of attitude that leads to an authentic  groove  before we move on here are some  additional remarks first of all last  minute i decided not to go with the  clavinet sound but with the wurlitzer  sound with the  guppy effect the wah effect  and i did that because i'm not used to  the clavinet sound and i'm not used to  the way it feels and sounds and i was  having trouble hearing certain pitches  the way i wanted them to sound with the  clavinet sound i think it's just a skill  and a touch that i just haven't acquired  yet  the type of strokes that you need to do  to get that slap sound  i'm not familiar with and it was it was  just hard for me to do also sustained  notes  i didn't like how it sounded with the  clavinet i much preferred  the wurlitzer  and quite simply i just preferred the  wurlitzer sound for this one  also because i'm very inexperienced when  it comes to funk music and new to the  genre it's just a bit awkward for me to  improvise some bits  because i'm just unfamiliar with that  kind of style where you're prioritizing  rhythm and focused on the groove  and there's just this attitude that i'm  very unfamiliar with  so that was a challenge but also very  fun  because it was a learning experience and  in terms of filming it was very fun  because first of all i was at the park  with bobby and  i'm never at the park so it was a nice  experience  but it was pretty challenging because  of a few things  the first thing was a keyboard setup  because i should have brought something  to elevate my keyboard but because it  was  near the ground i ended up putting a  towel there but it was still low because  it was low  it was really hard to play  the second thing is that there were  quite a quite a few people that kept  walking by and asking me questions or  talking to me  which  happens pretty often when i do these  videos but  not as often as as today yeah yeah okay  now here's the other thing if you're  using a tripod also i was having some  battery issues with the keyboard today  usually i put in a fresh set of  batteries before i do something like  this but today i just  didn't  and the thing about the keyboard is that  you can't tell when the battery is low  the only signal it gives you is that  maybe five minutes before  it's done it'll start to glitch and that  was happening luckily i got in a few  more takes before the keyboard died but  that was a little bit of a concern  it was my fault i should have put in a  fresh set of batteries  and now here's the final piece  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  hi bobby  hello

